title: Node.js Command Line With XCTDH HashHiding Markers
id: 9ffa244a-594a-42e9-833f-327be09646b6
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects Node.js launched with -eval strings carrying the XCTDH
    HashHiding indicators published by Ransom-ISAC (2026): the campaign
    marker global.i = '5-3-132' and the require-alias global.r=require used
    by the base-91, control-flow-flattened _Z module that decodes a C2
    endpoint from Ethereum recipient-address bytes.
references:
    - https://ransom-isac.org/blog/xctdh-adopts-hash-hiding/
    - https://opensourcemalware.com/blog/nullreceiver-dprk-c2-technique
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/09/29
tags:
    - attack.t1059
logsource:
    product: windows
    category: process_creation
detection:
    selection:
        CommandLine|contains:
            - 'global.i='
            - 'global.r=require'
    condition: selection
falsepositives:
    - Developer scripts or test harnesses that legitimately define the same
      globals (rare; correlate with a subsequent fetch to a bare IP endpoint)
level: high
